    "Description": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: xfrm: hold dev ref until after transport_finish NF_HOOK (CVE-2026-31663)\n\n* kernel: ALSA: 6fire: fix use-after-free on disconnect (CVE-2026-31581)\n\n* kernel: gfs2: Fix use-after-free in iomap inline data write path (CVE-2026-45984)\n\n* kernel: udf: fix partition descriptor append bookkeeping (CVE-2026-45991)\n\n* kernel: RDMA/rxe: Validate pad and ICRC before payload_size() in rxe_rcv (CVE-2026-46043)\n\n* kernel: RDMA/rxe: Reject unknown opcodes before ICRC processing (CVE-2026-46133)\n\n* kernel: sctp: purge outqueue on stale COOKIE-ECHO handling (CVE-2026-52924)\n\n* kernel: xfrm: policy: fix use-after-free on inexact bin in xfrm_policy_bysel_ctx() (CVE-2026-53239)\n\n* kernel: netfilter: synproxy: refresh tcphdr after skb_ensure_writable (CVE-2026-64007)\n\n* kernel: ip6: vti: Use ip6_tnl.net in vti6_siocdevprivate() (CVE-2026-63921)\n\n* kernel: xfrm: input: hold netns during deferred transport reinjection (CVE-2026-63919)\n\n* kernel: ip6: vti: Use ip6_tnl.net in vti6_changelink() (CVE-2026-63917)\n\n* kernel: RDMA/rxe: Fix a use-after-free problem in rxe_mmap (CVE-2026-64582)\n\n* kernel: net: qrtr: restrict socket creation to the initial network namespace (CVE-2026-68294)\n\n* kernel: xfrm: fix stale skb-\u003eprev after async crypto steals a GSO segment (CVE-2026-68426)\n\n* kernel: scsi: libiscsi_tcp: Bound SCSI Response data segment to the connection buffer (CVE-2026-74556)\n\n* kernel: netfilter: flowtable: publish GC-visible tuple last (CVE-2026-74746)\n\n* kernel: RDMA/rxe: Fix responder UAF on IB_QP_MAX_DEST_RD_ATOMIC modify_qp (CVE-2026-80864)\n\n* kernel: RDMA/rxe: Fix OOB in free_rd_atomic_resources() (CVE-2026-80863)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* xfs corruption from [xfs_trans_cancel] during inode allocation (JIRA:RHEL-257185)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
